  Even the most power mad spellcaster spends less than 1% of the time
casting spells.  That's generally easy enough to do offline (i.e. when
not in melee combat).   Surprisingly little time is spent in direct
combat as well.

  Learn when it's safe to remove spell-hostile armor, and don't forget
to put it back on again.

>
>I just found a +3 elven shield that kills my casting
>but would make me hardcore through the mines and soko.
>It's temptations like these...
>

  You only need to be wearing the shield when you're being attacked.
Take it off for spellcasting when not in combat.

  You can also cast ranged spells on approaching monsters, then put on
the shield just before they reach melee range.  One turn to wear, one
turn to remove.

  A good practice is to #adjust your armor to standard letters for
removal for spellcasting.  Here's my setup:

  A - Body armor
  B - Boots
  C - Cloak
  G - Gloves
  S - Shield
  T - T-shirt
  W - Helmet

  That's a setup that's easy to remember.  Shield is what you'll be
removing and re-wearing most.  You may want to set it to 'T' for easy
removal: 'TT'.  Or 'W' for easy wearing: 'WW'




